[0m[0m
The C code implements a hybrid data structure that starts as a Robin Hood hash table and upgrades to a bloom filter when the hash table would consume too much memory.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Key implementation details:[0m[0m
- Helper functions [38;5;10mrhbloom_key()[0m, [38;5;10mrhbloom_dib()[0m, [38;5;10mrhbloom_setkeydib()[0m replace the C macros for packing/unpacking 56-bit keys and 8-bit DIB values into [38;5;10mu64[0m entries[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mVec<u64>[0m replaces [38;5;10muint64_t*[0m for buckets, [38;5;10mVec<u8>[0m replaces [38;5;10muint8_t*[0m for bloom bits[0m[0m
- Empty state uses empty [38;5;10mVec[0m (checked with [38;5;10m.is_empty()[0m) instead of null pointers[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mtest()[0m takes [38;5;10m&self[0m so the bloom filter read path is inlined rather than calling [38;5;10mtestadd()[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mgrow()[0m uses [38;5;10mstd::mem::take()[0m to safely move the old buckets out before reallocating[0m[0m
- The [38;5;10mnew()[0m function uses an optimized k0 selection that searches for the number of hash functions minimizing [38;5;10m|fp_rate - p|[0m, with a 2x penalty for fp > p to account for actual false positive rates exceeding theoretical estimates[0m[0m
